WEBVTT

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.150
C'mon now!!

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:12.220
Get a hold of yourself!!

00:00:12.380 --> 00:00:13.850
There's another trap, Yuma!

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:14.860
Wha-?

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:20.280
Hurry, Yuma!!

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:25.930
We're safe...

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:30.100
Ugh!! What is wrong with you, Yuma?!

00:00:31.250 --> 00:00:31.970
Yuma?

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:35.680
Droite...

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.010
Kaito...

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:38.390
IV...

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:39.760
V...

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:41.180
...and now Shark...

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:43.210
I'll...

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.740
In front of you, Yuma!!

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.790
Whoa, what's this place?

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:04.120
It seems that this is our battlefield.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.670
I've been waiting.

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:14.730
Wait, you're...

00:01:16.820 --> 00:01:17.600
Gauche!

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.120
Alright, satisfy me, Yuma!!

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.060
With our Duel, that is!

00:01:24.830 --> 00:01:29.880
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.220
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:01:48.070 --> 00:01:52.070
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:57.870
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:02.460
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:08.500
<i>It's too late for us to turn back now</i>

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:13.590
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.140
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:24.940
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:29.980
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:35.450
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.120
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.290
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:53.380
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:02:55.270 --> 00:02:57.940
<i>Heart Burning!!</i>

00:02:58.820 --> 00:03:01.200
<i>So who will be the last entrant in the finals?!</i>

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.240
<i>Will it be Yuma Tsukumo or will it be Gauche?!</i>

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.200
<i>The field the two will be battling in...</i>

00:03:08.750 --> 00:03:10.670
<i>...is the Dangerous Canyon!!</i>

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:12.290
Let's go!!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:13.460
Yeah!!

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:19.170
Number 59: A Fierce Fight! Yuma VS Gauche:
 This is My Manly Dueling Soul!"

00:03:17.460 --> 00:03:18.050
--Duel!!
 --Duel!!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.300
I'll take the first move!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.810
It's my turn! Draw!!

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.600
I Summon Heroic Challenger - Double Lance!

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.950
<i>Whoa! Due to the Field Magic's effects,</i>

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.530
<i>Gauche has suddenly received 200 points of damage!</i>

00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:53.040
<i>Due to this field, when a Monster is Summoned or declares an attack,</i>

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:56.960
<i>The player receives 200 points of damage!</i>

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:01.420
So the more you attack, the more your Life is depleted?

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:03.590
Wha-? That's really bad!

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:06.430
And I only have 100 Life points to boot!

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:13.140
How was it? Did you like my little present, Gauche-<i>kun</i>?

00:04:15.150 --> 00:04:18.440
I get it. So that's your little gimmick, huh?

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:29.830
<i>When Droite and I were kids, we were picked up by Mr. Heartland.</i>

00:04:30.580 --> 00:04:34.000
<i>He then taught us how to Duel and always did what we asked.</i>

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:38.290
<i>But after seeing his--Yuma's Dueling style,</i>

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.920
<i>it reignited my burning Dueling spirit!</i>

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:46.140
These are the Duels I crave for!!

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.430
Double Lance's effect activates!

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.390
When used to Xyz Summon a Heroic Champion,

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:55.100
it counts as two materials.

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:59.020
I Overlay my now <i>two</i> Level Four Double Lances!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.610
I build the Overlay Network and Xyz Summon!

00:05:05.570 --> 00:05:09.200
Come forth!
 Heroic Champion - Gandiva!!

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.080
He completely disregarded the Field Magic's effect damage.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:21.090
Now I set two cards face-down and end my turn!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:23.840
Now bring it, Yuma!

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.180
Show me that spirit of yours!

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.760
Man, that Gauche!

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.350
<i>I can't attack blindly due to how low my Life is.</i>

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:37.230
Why are you hesitating, Yuma?

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.900
He's all pumped up.

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:42.320
If we don't do our best...

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.240
I get what you're trying to say!

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.780
It's my turn! Draw!

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.070
And now you'll take my Trap!

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:52.160
A-Ah crap!

00:05:52.410 --> 00:05:52.790
Here it comes!

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.330
Heroic Gift.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.830
When my opponent's Life is less than 2000,

00:05:58.460 --> 00:05:59.960
it changes it to 4000 Life.

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:05.460
Why did he boost my Life?

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:08.800
Then I can draw two cards!

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.720
Why'd he change Yuma's Life to 4000?

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:15.100
The hell is this all about, pal?!

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:16.810
Don't get me wrong.

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:19.730
All I wanted was to draw some cards.

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:23.730
Besides, it's not my style to hunt down weak prey.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.610
Why you!!

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.110
<i>To think that Gauche gave Yuma some Life...</i>

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.990
<i>He's giving his all in this Duel, it seems.</i>

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:37.120
I set a Monster in Face-Down Defense Mode!

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:42.080
Yuma, you can't win against him with just defending!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.840
It's fine! I got a little plan of my own!

00:06:46.590 --> 00:06:49.180
I now set a card and end my turn!

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.890
Heh, taking quite the defensive stance, aren't you?

00:06:52.260 --> 00:06:54.640
It's my turn! Draw!

00:06:55.390 --> 00:06:59.350
I Summon Heroic Challenger - Night-Attack Kantera!

00:07:07.860 --> 00:07:11.030
Alright! He got 200 more damage!

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.120
So what?!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.120
I use Night-Attack Kantera to attack your Face-Down Monster!

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:23.000
This card...

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.460
...can destroy a Monster in Face-Down Defense Mode...

00:07:25.920 --> 00:07:28.130
...without conducting Battle Damage!

00:07:33.510 --> 00:07:35.970
Now your field is empty!

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:39.060
Gandiva can attack you directly now!

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.440
I was waiting for that!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:42.100
What?!

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:47.900
When Mog Mole is destroyed, it can be Special Summoned in Face-Up Defense Mode!

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.400
That little attack that cost you 400 Life Points...

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.740
...was all a waste!

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.950
Why you! You ruined the mood!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:59.790
I activate Gandiva's effect!

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:02.830
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:08:03.330 --> 00:08:07.590
I can destroy a Level Four or lower Monster that was Special Summoned!

00:08:09.210 --> 00:08:09.880
What?!

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:20.100
If you're gonna fight cowardly, I'll crush you!

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:23.940
Now go, Gandiva! Direct Attack!!

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:27.360
Trap, activate! Battle Break!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.360
It destroys the battling Monster...

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.860
...and ends the battle!

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:35.610
Stop defending this mood!

00:08:36.030 --> 00:08:38.530
Trap, activate! Battler's Pride!

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:41.950
It negates and destroys a card that ends the Battle Phase!

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.920
Now go, Gandiva!!

00:08:54.550 --> 00:08:57.180
I set a card and end my turn.

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:01.720
You get it now?

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:04.980
You can't beat me with that spirit of yours!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.980
But I can't afford to lose this Duel!

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:14.570
Yuma, you just can't win this Duel.

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:15.150
Say what?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:20.330
Now that you're being too cautious, you fear winning in this Duel.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:21.490
Huh?

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.420
It's probably from watching Kaito's and Shark's Duels.

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:31.340
Due to you watching, you must've developed a fear of Dueling.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:34.970
You think I'm afraid?!

00:09:36.180 --> 00:09:37.800
It's my turn! Draw!

00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:39.930
Am I wrong...?

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:42.600
I'll...

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:45.770
I Summon Gagaga Magician!!

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:58.570
And from my hand, I activate One-Shot Wand!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:05.120
This card raises the Attack Power of a Magician-Type Monster by 800 points!

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.330
Now Gagaga Magician's Attack Power is higher!

00:10:09.580 --> 00:10:11.710
Go, Gagaga Magician!

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:14.800
Attack Gandiva!!

00:10:16.300 --> 00:10:18.630
This mood won't work with me!

00:10:19.260 --> 00:10:21.800
Trap, activate! Heroic Advance!

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:24.310
Because you attacked Heroic Champion,

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:28.140
a Heroic Challenger's Attack Power is doubled,

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.480
and becomes the attack target!

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:35.780
However, the Monsters aren't destroyed!!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.910
I activate One-Shot Wand's effect!

00:10:48.370 --> 00:10:51.040
By destroying this card when a battle has finished,

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:54.210
I can draw one card!

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.510
Alright! I Summon Grandran!

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.550
When there is an Xyz Monster on my opponent's field,

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.930
I can Special Summon him from my hand in Attack Mode!

00:11:07.020 --> 00:11:12.270
And now I Overlay my Level Four Gagaga Magician and Grandran!

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.860
I build the Overlay Network!

00:11:14.860 --> 00:11:16.530
Xyz Summon!

00:11:17.190 --> 00:11:19.780
Come forth!!
 Gagaga Gunman!

00:11:22.910 --> 00:11:25.660
What? In Defense Mode?!

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:30.250
It's obvious that he put him in Defense Mode to avoid taking damage from the Field Magic.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.130
When Gagaga Gunman is in Defense Mode,

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:36.500
once per turn, by detaching an Overlay Unit,

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.670
I inflict 800 points of damage to my opponent!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:47.180
I did it! How 'bout that, Gauche?!

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:51.100
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.980
How 'bout that? That was such a cheap attack!

00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:57.730
I don't...

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:01.530
I don't wanna have such a lame Duel with you!

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:05.120
It's my turn! Draw!

00:12:05.870 --> 00:12:10.120
From my hand, I activate the Equip Magic, Xyz Crowned Jewel!

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:17.170
This card makes the Xyz Monster's Rank to a Level and is treated as two Xyz Material.

00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:21.470
What? Using an Xyz Monster to Xyz Summon?

00:12:21.920 --> 00:12:27.550
I Overlay my Level Four Night-Attack Kantera and my, now <i>two</i> Gandivas!

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.720
I build the Overlay Network!

00:12:30.720 --> 00:12:32.390
Xyz Summon!

00:12:33.770 --> 00:12:37.940
Come forth!
 Heroic Champion - Kusanagi!

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:53.040
Bring it!!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:55.620
If you really wish to defeat me,

00:12:56.130 --> 00:12:57.540
show how you truly Duel!

00:12:57.960 --> 00:12:59.000
Come at me!!

00:12:59.800 --> 00:13:01.130
How I truly Duel?

00:13:01.460 --> 00:13:04.430
Yes! The <i>true</i> way to Duel!!

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.550
I see what he means...

00:13:09.310 --> 00:13:12.220
Now matter the circumstance, Gauche kept his Dueling style as is.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:15.190
But all I've done...

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:18.900
<i>I set a Monster in Face-Down Defense Mode!</i>

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:20.820
<i>How 'bout that, Gauche?!</i>

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:25.610
Yuma...

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:38.500
What are you doing, Yuma?

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:40.710
Get off, Kotori.

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:43.210
I'm going alone from here on out.

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:43.920
Wha-?

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:45.300
Please!

00:13:46.800 --> 00:13:47.630
The way he Duels...

00:13:48.220 --> 00:13:51.180
I gotta give it my all against him, got it?

00:13:52.140 --> 00:13:52.890
Yuma...

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:01.440
Well go win and pick me up afterwards.

00:14:01.980 --> 00:14:02.570
Yeah!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:07.200
Go for it, Yuma!

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:12.660
There's no doubt that Shark and Kaito are strong.

00:14:13.160 --> 00:14:14.830
They also possess fearsome power.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.040
To people like them, even you are feeling fear,

00:14:18.580 --> 00:14:20.750
I can understand how you feel enough.

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:25.260
But haven't you always overcome that fear, and come all this way?

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:28.180
Astral... Let's go.

00:14:29.220 --> 00:14:33.350
In the end, I have to Duel in my own way!

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:34.810
Yuma...

00:14:37.430 --> 00:14:38.230
Gauche!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:42.520
Now I will let you to see my <i>real</i> Dueling!

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:46.320
Oh! So you're finally acting serious!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:47.570
Let's do this!

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.660
I activate the Magic Card from my hand, Fighter’s Charm!

00:14:54.280 --> 00:14:57.830
This card can switch a Monster from Defense Position to Attack Position!

00:14:58.290 --> 00:15:01.580
But this turn, its Attack Power becomes the same as its Defense Power!

00:15:03.290 --> 00:15:08.340
Then I attack Gagaga Gunman with the 2500 Attack Power Kusanagi!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.890
I activate a Trap, Overlay Burst!

00:15:19.640 --> 00:15:26.150
Until the End Phase, this card increase one Monster’s Attack Power by 500!

00:15:28.610 --> 00:15:29.820
I got this!

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:31.530
Don't be so sure!

00:15:32.200 --> 00:15:37.580
By detaching one Overlay Unit, Kusanagi can negate the activation and effect of a Trap Card,

00:15:38.080 --> 00:15:41.170
and gain 500 Attack Points during this turn!

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.790
3000 Attack Points?!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.630
Finish it, Kusanagi!

00:15:50.970 --> 00:15:52.550
Their difference in Attack Power is now reversed!

00:15:53.260 --> 00:15:56.930
Go, Kusanagi! Attack Gagaga Gunman!

00:15:57.470 --> 00:16:01.480
Dream on! I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Fighting Bond!

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:04.480
It negates one Monster’s destruction in battle!

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:10.320
But you still receive damage!

00:16:14.700 --> 00:16:17.370
I set two cards, and end my turn!

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:20.580
Hmph! Now you only have 600 Life left.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.710
About ready to give up?

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.500
What are you talking about?

00:16:24.960 --> 00:16:27.380
The real match begins now!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.220
That's it! That's the mood I wanted from you all along!

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:49.150
What?!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:50.730
The heck?!

00:16:51.150 --> 00:16:52.530
It's a new Field Magic.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.860
Battleground of the Setting Sun.

00:16:55.660 --> 00:16:57.700
You can only battle with one Monster.

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.910
When a Monster is destroyed,

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.910
it inflicts 300 points of damage to that player.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.120
Let's do this... Yuma!

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:07.580
Heck yeah!

00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:10.000
My turn! Draw!

00:17:10.800 --> 00:17:13.550
I attack Kusanagi with Gagaga Gunman!

00:17:14.090 --> 00:17:16.180
What can you do with that guy?!

00:17:16.840 --> 00:17:18.760
Mine has higher Attack Power!

00:17:19.220 --> 00:17:21.640
When Gagaga Gunman is in Attack Position,

00:17:21.930 --> 00:17:26.060
by detaching one Overlay Unit, it gains 1000 Attack Points,

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:29.770
and lowers the Monster my opponent controls by 500!

00:17:31.650 --> 00:17:32.900
Not too bad.

00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.650
Go, Gagaga Gunmen!

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:37.320
I activate a Trap, Heroic Change!

00:17:37.780 --> 00:17:40.370
Then I activate Kusanagi’s Monster Effect!

00:17:40.870 --> 00:17:43.410
I negate the Trap I just activated,

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.580
and increase Kusanagi’s Attack Power by 500!

00:17:59.640 --> 00:18:00.640
A draw...

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.180
To think you defeated my Kusanagi...

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:06.060
Yuma, you're not half bad!

00:18:06.890 --> 00:18:08.150
Right back at you!

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:15.110
But this will be our final battle!

00:18:15.650 --> 00:18:18.410
I activate a Trap, Xyz Hotblooded Battle!

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:21.280
When an Xyz Monster is destroyed by battle,

00:18:21.740 --> 00:18:27.580
by paying 1000 LP, both players can use the destroyed Xyz Monster as the material,

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.630
and Special Summon an Xyz Monster with the same rank!

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.590
Special Summon?

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:38.880
Come forth! Heroic Champion Excalibur!

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:52.440
But the Xyz Monster Summoned by this effect will be destroyed after the battle!

00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:56.070
So bring it, Yuma!
 It's your turn now!

00:18:56.400 --> 00:18:58.490
Summon Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:58.860 --> 00:18:59.740
Hope?!

00:19:00.410 --> 00:19:02.240
It won't be any fun if you don't, right?

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:04.910
Let's both duke it out with our aces!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:07.870
He wants to fight against a Number?

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:13.210
Fine... I accept your challenge!

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:15.630
Come!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.760
Come forth! Number 39!

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:22.340
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.930
Now bring it on!

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:33.230
Yeah! Aspiring Emperor - Hope attacks Excalibur!

00:19:33.440 --> 00:19:35.820
I activate Excalibur's effect!

00:19:36.530 --> 00:19:39.530
During a battle, I detach all of its Overlay Units

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:41.820
to double its Attack Power!

00:19:46.200 --> 00:19:47.620
It's got 4000 Attack Points!

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.120
I activate Hope's effect!

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.290
Rune Barrier!!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:00.800
He protected me!

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:03.640
Still, once the battle ends,

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:06.640
due to Xyz Hotblooded Battle’s effect, the Monsters will be destroyed!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:12.100
And thanks to the Field Magic's effect, you will take 300 points of damage and lose!

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.940
No... I still have this card!

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:17.070
What!?

00:20:17.690 --> 00:20:19.990
I'm gonna bring it to ya!

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:24.610
I activate the Quick-Play Magic from my hand, Double-Up Chance!

00:20:25.200 --> 00:20:27.530
When a Monster’s attack is negated,

00:20:27.870 --> 00:20:31.620
it can double its Attack Power and attack once again!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.920
What?! 5000 Attack Points?!

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:41.840
Go! Hope Sword Double Slash!!

00:20:49.430 --> 00:20:51.390
<i>It is decided!</i>

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:53.980
<i>The one who advanced to the Final is…</i>

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:56.350
<i>Yuma Tsukumo!</i>

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.110
Tsukumo...

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:03.400
Yuma...

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:07.700
Sorry, Droite... I lost...

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:09.870
Gauche!

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:15.620
As expected, your mood is simply great.

00:21:16.290 --> 00:21:17.290
I had a blast!

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:18.130
Yeah!

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:23.050
Yuma, take this with you.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:23.760
Huh?

00:21:24.050 --> 00:21:27.140
In exchange, if I ever catch you Dueling without a good mood...

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:29.430
I'll beat the hell outta you!

00:21:30.310 --> 00:21:30.970
This is...

00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:32.470
Excalibur?!

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:34.770
But this card...

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:38.940
What we call a “Duelist” also means to inherit the loser’s feelings.

00:21:39.270 --> 00:21:43.610
He entrusted his feeling towards Dueling to you.

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:50.700
Thank you, Gauche. I'll definitely inherit your feelings!

00:21:51.240 --> 00:21:53.750
Yeah! Please do, Yuma!

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:56.460
Do your best!

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:08.640
Gosh, Yuma! Get back here!

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:15.480
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:21.110
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:31.780
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:36.080
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.330
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.580 --> 00:22:40.040
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.210 --> 00:22:42.670
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:47.880
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.050 --> 00:22:53.220
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.350 --> 00:22:58.850
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.230 --> 00:23:05.360
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.530 --> 00:23:10.820
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:16.120
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.330 --> 00:23:21.710
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:21.710 --> 00:23:26.920
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.130 --> 00:23:32.470
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:42.520
It's the Duel Carnival Tournament Finals!

00:23:42.520 --> 00:23:47.230
The ones who advanced are: Kaito, Shark, Tron, and me!

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:50.200
No matter who my opponent is, I have to find a way to win!

00:23:50.200 --> 00:23:52.910
Huh? My deck's gone!

00:23:52.910 --> 00:23:55.120
God, you're such an idiot!

00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:56.870
Haruto is above us.

00:23:56.870 --> 00:23:58.500
Just leave this to us!

00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.960
You… Are you really okay with this?!

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:03.500
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:07.050
"The Overture Towards the Final Battle:
 The New Foe Dr. Faker!"

00:24:07.670 --> 00:24:09.420
You're Dr. Faker?

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:15.140
Here's today's introduction!
 Straight out of the Gagaga Academy, our new friend, Gagaga Gunman!

00:24:15.550 --> 00:24:17.890
Gagaga Academy? When did we name it that?

00:24:18.100 --> 00:24:20.480
And we nominated you as the university's principle!

00:24:21.020 --> 00:24:22.480
I'm Principle Astral.

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:23.440
You really did become it!
